 content=\"630\"/><script src=\"/_next/static/chunks/polyfills-42372ed130431b0a.js\" noModule=\"\"></script></head><body><div hidden=\"\"><!--$--><!--/$--></div><main class=\"max-w-2xl mx-auto px-6 py-20\"><a class=\"text-neutral-500 hover:text-neutral-200 text-sm transition-colors mb-10 inline-block\" href=\"/\">← back</a><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mb-3\"><h1 class=\"text-2xl font-normal text-neutral-100\">Quantitative Trading Research</h1><span class=\"inline-block text-xs px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-mono tracking-wide bg-amber-950 text-amber-400 border border-amber-900\">in-progress</span></div><p class=\"text-neutral-500 text-sm mb-8\">A backtesting framework for evaluating quantitative trading strategies on public market data.</p><div class=\"flex gap-2 mb-10 flex-wrap\"><span class=\"inline-block text-xs px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-mono tracking-wide bg-transparent text-neutral-500 border border-neutral-800\">python</span><span class=\"inline-block text-xs px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-mono tracking-wide bg-transparent text-neutral-500 border border-neutral-800\">finance</span><span class=\"inline-block text-xs px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-mono tracking-wide bg-transparent text-neutral-500 border border-neutral-800\">data</span></div><article class=\"prose prose-invert prose-sm max-w-none prose-neutral\"><h2>Overview</h2>\n<p>Building a backtesting framework for evaluating quantitative trading strategies on public market data (Yahoo Finance). The project covers data ingestion, strategy evaluation, and performance metrics.</p>\n<h2>Scope</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Data handling</strong> — loading, cleaning, and structuring time series market data</li>\n<li><strong>Strategy implementation</strong> — baseline strategies including momentum and moving average crossovers</li>\n<li><strong>Evaluation</strong> — PnL computation, returns, volatility, and drawdown metrics</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Status</h2>\n<p>In progress. No live trading involved.</p></article></main><!--$--><!--/$-